# Commit and push at the end of the conversation

When a conversation changes files in this repo, finish by committing and pushing. Do this in the same turn as the work, before the final reply.

1. If there is nothing to commit, stop. Do not create an empty commit.
2. Review `git status`, `git diff`, and recent `git log` messages. Follow the existing `fix:` / `feat:` style.
3. Stage the relevant files. Leave out secrets (`.env`, credentials, keys).
4. Commit with a message that says why the change exists.
5. Push the current branch to `origin` with `git push`. Do not force-push.

Do not update git config, skip hooks, or amend a commit that was not created in this conversation.
